From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SettingsProvider: additional instances share the first one's state

ActivityThread constructs a provider instance for whichever system thread
asks for "settings" first and another one in installSystemProviders(); it
keeps one, but onCreate() has run on both. Each instance owned a separate
in-memory copy of the settings and the same files, and the "settings"
service was registered by whichever onCreate() finished last. On PW3 Test
V29 the ActivityManager thread and the main thread both created one
(two SettingsProvider threads, two "No settings state" lines 33 ms apart):
cmd settings wrote 1800000 to screen_off_timeout while PowerManager kept
reading 60000 from the other copy, so the screen slept every minute.

Further instances now adopt the lock and state of the first. They wait at
most 20 s for it, then fall back to the previous behaviour. onCreate() logs
its stack so the early caller can be identified.

